{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Intro over verse
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In the [E]darkness of the [B]night, all I hear is a [A]ringing in [B]my [E]ears;
And my [A]eyes are full of [E]tears that I can't [B]see.
And I'll seek [C#m]comfort in bad [B]places, and I'm [A]trying to [B]forget the [E]faces,
Of the [A]many friends who [E]say, “that it was [B]never meant to [E]be.”
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
And you can [E]always write if off by [B]saying, that it was [A]never [B]meant to [E]be,
Though you [A]once told me we'd [E]always be as [B]one.
And then you [C#m]wish me a better [B]day as you [A]turn your [G#m]back [C#m]away,
And then you [A]write it off by [E]saying, "It was [B]never meant to [E]be."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Well, it left some damage in my wake, but I have the liberty to take the time
to say, "It ain't all my fault alone
I've been deceived and I've been forced to leave my anger and my greaving
In a heart that’s still believing, it was always meant to be."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
You have turned your beauty and your charm into a weapon to badly harm
The man you said was the best friend you have known.
Then, your ways are justified by stubborn, foolish pride.
And the price is paid by me, because that's the way it’s meant to be.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
There is no dignity in remaining; love ain't worth retaining
anymore, so let’s just do each other in.
And leave the sadness and the fury, to the judgment of a jury,
and the signature that's saying, "It was never meant to be."
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
And then you [C#m]wish me a better [B]day as you [A]turn your [G#m]back [C#m]away from me,
And then you [A]write it off by [E]saying, "It was [B]never meant to [A]be."[E]
{end_of_chorus}
